316 0 obj
<<
/Title (Low-code development is an approach to building software applications mainly through visual tools and configuration instead of writing large amounts of traditional program code. Applications are assembled using visual development environments, predefined components and templates. Typical building blocks include forms for capturing data, reports and dashboards for viewing it, and workflows that define how information moves through a business process. Zoho Creator is an example of such a platform, in which applications are built from forms, reports and workflows and can be extended with Deluge scripting.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 252 0 R
/Next 317 0 R
>>
endobj
317 0 obj
<<
/Title (Automation is a central feature of low-code platforms. Rules, triggers and scheduled actions can perform repetitive tasks without manual effort. Because much of the routine programming is handled by the platform, development effort is reduced and applications can be delivered faster. Low-code platforms are also accessible to a wider group of people: professional developers use them to speed up their work, and business users with limited programming)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 252 0 R
/Prev 316 0 R
>>
endobj
